---
import LegalPage from "~/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { localeParams, useTranslations } from "~/i18n";
import { toLanguage } from "~/i18n/config";
import { SITE } from "~/data/site";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return localeParams();
}

const language = toLanguage(Astro.params.lang);
const t = useTranslations(language);
---

<LegalPage
  language={language}
  path="legal/refund"
  title={t("legal.refund")}
  metaTitle={t("legal.meta.refund")}
  description="TenPrint Software's 30-day, no-questions-asked refund policy for paid licences."
>
  <p>
    Every paid {SITE.name} licence can be refunded in full within <strong>30 days</strong> of purchase,
    for any reason. You do not have to justify the request, and we will not try to talk you out of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why the policy is this generous</h2>
  <p>
    Every application is free to download and offers a real trial before you pay anything, so you can
    find out whether it fits your workflow without spending money. If you still decide after buying
    that it is not for you, we would rather return the payment than keep it.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> from the address you used at checkout.
    </li>
    <li>Include the order number from your purchase confirmation, or the licence key.</li>
    <li>You do not need to explain why, though we always appreciate knowing what went wrong.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process refunds within three working days of receiving the request. The money is returned by
    our merchant of record to the original payment method; how quickly it appears depends on your bank
    or card issuer, typically five to ten working days.
  </p>

  <h2>After a refund</h2>
  <p>
    The associated licence key is deactivated when the refund is issued. The application itself keeps
    working with its free feature set — nothing is uninstalled and none of your settings or data are
    removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Beyond 30 days</h2>
  <p>
    We are not obliged to refund a purchase older than 30 days, but we look at genuine cases
    individually. If an application stops working because of a defect we introduced and we cannot fix
    it in a reasonable time, write to us regardless of how long ago you bought it.
  </p>

  <h2>Statutory rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a consumer in the European Union, this policy sits on top of your statutory 14-day right
    of withdrawal for distance contracts and never replaces it. Where the two differ, whichever gives
    you more applies.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
